WEBVTT

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:16.620
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:27.630
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:33.170
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:38.670
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.580
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:49.380
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:54.420
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.830
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:11.150
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:23.390
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.940
I think I had a little too
much to drink, hehe...

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.320
Wha?

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.870
Foolish man! People like you
perpetuate evil in society.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.380
You will spend the night
there and sober up!

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.670
FILE. 7
STRIKE MAN -
DEFENDER OF
JUSTICE?

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.980
Come on, get yourself together.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.680
Come on, get yourself together.
I was up late, fixing "Today."

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.380
What's all this, so early
in the morning?

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.180
Oh, my...

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:09.180
"This drunk has been judged a criminal
for urinating on this telephone pole."

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.230
How can you get so close
to him, Miyuki?!

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.590
"Superhero Strike Man"

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:15.900
"Superhero..."

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.700
"Strike Man?!"

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.850
I am Strike Man, evil's
worst nightmare!

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:34.860
"Motorized Entry Restricted To Residents"

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:39.590
Using this alley, where children play,
as a short cut... It's inexcusable!

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.420
You're such wholesome
youths...

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.800
...so I'll give you a special memento,
my autographed baseball!

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.730
What?! It is not necessary
to thank justice!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.280
What am I supposed to do with this?

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.010
What am I supposed to do with this?
What a dork!

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.270
Damn!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.350
It's caught...

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.450
For justice in
the world...

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.080
...and to combat the rampant chaos of
neglected bicycles at train stations.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:11.390
Divine Retribution!

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.360
Divine Retribution!
Aah! My bike!

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.960
I'm on a mission from God to fight
evil! If I don't do it, who will?

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:28.200
Loitering in a public phone booth is
inexcusable!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.040
Silence! I am
justice!

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.080
Huh?

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:43.250
Behold! 'Tis the vengeance
of heaven!

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.200
Jump!

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.420
Hear me well, Ignorer
of Red Lights!

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.660
The heavens may forgive you, but Strike
Man can never permit such a crime!

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.170
"Strike Man Delivers Blow to
Driver Who Ran Red Light"

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.510
What on earth
is this?!

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.810
It's like he's some kind
of superhero.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.650
They write all these things without
considering what we go through.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.850
Did you finish
that report?

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:18.120
Finish?! Not even close! You
have to help me, too!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.850
We've got trouble! Yoriko's been
assaulted by the Strike Man!

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:23.760
What'd you say?!

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:33.760
It was scary!

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.100
All right, all right,
you're okay now.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.270
How dare he do this in front
of our police station?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:43.780
"Notice; This man has been
judged to be a pervert."

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.780
You did see the
culprit, right?

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:51.520
He's the culprit! I was waiting in line
for the bus, and he flashed me!

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:54.660
No, no, we're talking
about Strike Man.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.020
Strike Man?

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:00.260
He came storming by
on his motorbike...

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:04.000
...quickly resolved the problem,
and then was off like the wind!

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:04.970
Now, listen...

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.840
What kind of bike? And the plate was?

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.770
I don't know...

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.380
Motorbikes all look
the same to me.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:11.580
D'oh...

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.550
Duh...

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:24.020
Bokuto Station calling patrol car 4.
Bokuto Station calling patrol car 4.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.350
This is patrol
car 4, over...

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.360
Accident involving a taxi and truck near
the west entrance of Bokuto Park.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.600
We have a report that the
drivers are arguing.

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:36.400
Roger! Proceeding
to the scene!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.070
I'm glad that Strike Man isn't
involved in this one.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.410
Absolutely...

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.070
"Bokuto Park"

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.980
Somehow... I have a bad feeling
about this.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:59.020
"Both sides punished for fighting...
Superhero Strike Man."

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.990
Ah! I knew it!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.460
That Strike
Bastard.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.260
How dare he take the law
into his own hands!

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:08.960
"Both sides punished
for fighting?"

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.800
How can he justify using violence
to punish violence?

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.390
We've been tied up quite a bit
by that Strike Man lately.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.990
And we still have
no leads.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:36.650
Well, we should do some shopping
to get our minds off him.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.900
I'll go buy the parking
ticket.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.880
Where did we arrange
to meet Aoi?

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:58.510
The Eldorado, by the train station. Right
here by the vending machines.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.550
I think we're a
little early.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:06.730
Well, shall we go
ahead then?

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:09.380
Sure.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.160
I just can't get over
this jet lag.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.000
I stayed in Detroit for a
very, very long time.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.240
No. I must get
a grip...

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:28.870
There is no night or day for a
defender of justice. Huh?

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.610
What's this
all about?!

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.780
Don't these people know
what this sign means?!

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.930
Strike Screw-
driver!

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.330
Strike Air
Release!

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.610
Huh?

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.980
Someone left their
change...

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.440
Misappropriation, huh?

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:06.310
She may be a beautiful woman, but I
cannot bring myself to forgive her!

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:08.610
I will have to give her
a stern warning!

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:13.390
Excuse me! I think you
forgot your change.

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.790
Well, thank you
so very much...

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:20.290
Well! A rare show of kindness
in this day and age, Miss!

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.230
Please put out your
hand, my fair lady.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:29.100
"Strike Man"

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:32.710
I present this to you
as a reward.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.780
Never lose that kind
spirit of yours.

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:47.290
W... What on earth?

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:49.160
Oh, sorry...

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:50.760
Oh, sorry...
Have you waited long, Aoi?

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:50.900
Have you waited long, Aoi?

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.030
Not at all.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.430
Hmm? What's that?

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:57.270
Strike Man was just here...

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:58.740
Strike Man?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.970
Which way did he go?!

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:02.340
Uh... that
way.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.440
We might be able to
catch up to him.

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:06.340
Natsumi, we should
go after him by car.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:15.320
Hey, who let
the air out?

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:24.460
"Justice"

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:26.690
A Strike Man No Parking
Sticker?!
"Justice"

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:26.730
A Strike Man No Parking
Sticker?!

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:29.900
We bought a ticket, and
it hasn't expired yet!

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.970
This time you've gone
too far, Strike Man...

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:34.170
Oh, my precious Toyota
hatchback!

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.470
You'll be sorry,
Strike Man!

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:47.010
I will never, ever forgive
you for this!

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.230
"Bokuto Station Cafeteria"

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.560
Okay, we'll go over the physical char-
acteristics of the Strike Man again.

00:10:58.730 --> 00:10:59.230
Right.

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:00.700
We appreciate it.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:05.530
Well, he's pretty solid and muscular,
and about 180 cm tall.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:09.540
He was wearing a funny mask which hid
his face. And he also wore a cape.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.500
He's about 180 cm
and muscular.

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:15.510
A mask and a cape... so
we can't see his face.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:19.790
And he rides in on his motorcycle,
and disappears like the wind!

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:27.250
Nakajima?
Nakajima?

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:28.090
Huh?

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:29.080
Huh?
No way!

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:33.290
Oh, it's possible! Even Nakajima has a
very strong sense of justice at times.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:36.760
Hey, what's up? You
all look so puzzled.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.940
You're right! It's gotta be him! Even
the tone of his voice is the same!

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:43.040
Huh?

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:46.180
Hey, Nakajima... Say "Farewell,
Hahaha!"

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.010
"Farewell, Hahaha?"

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:52.980
I knew it, it's Nakajima! I'm
sure he's Strike Man!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.320
Where were you two nights ago?

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.260
Where were you two nights ago?
I was sleeping at home.

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:00.390
I was sleeping at home.

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:02.260
How about 7;30 yesterday morning?

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:04.160
I was just waking up.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.730
Can anyone confirm that?

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:07.460
Of course not.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:11.590
I believe you were patrolling the area near
the station at 10 yesterday morning.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:12.360
Yes.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:16.130
At Bokuto Bridge first thing that morning,
Bokuto Park at 3 in the afternoon...

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:20.910
...an alley behind River Road in the even-
ing, and on Mito Avenue at night.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:24.580
And you don't have an
alibi for any of them!

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:28.780
Give me a break! Motorcycle
patrols are always done solo.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:32.650
But why did you have to do something
so stupid? The trouble we had...

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.990
Wait a minute! I'm
not Strike Man!

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:38.890
We shall not dismiss this lightly,
despite your esteemed stature!

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.400
Confess, fella!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.560
Confess, fella!
You watch too much samurai cinema.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.930
Come on, let's forgive
him this time.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:48.910
Nakajima is the personification of justice,
even when not in uniform.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:50.900
Kobayakawa!

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.840
This isn't the kind of thing you
should dismiss out of hand.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:59.280
You intended no
harm, right?

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:02.440
Kobayakawa. Even you?
You think that I'm...

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.360
Boo Hoo!

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:15.470
I was kidding! Nakajima
isn't Strike Man.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:16.300
What?!

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:18.070
What?!
Whatcha mean "What?!"

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:20.930
But Nakajima doesn't
have a good alibi.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:22.630
It's right
here.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.970
Just look. Nakajima's handwriting
is nowhere as good as this.

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:37.050
"Iogi Travels"

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.390
<i>"Handwriting analysis, huh? That</i>
<i>never occurred to me."</i>

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:44.660
<i>"We should've noticed</i>
<i>it right away."</i>

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:48.860
<i>"Way to go, Nakajima! I always</i>
<i>knew that you were innocent!"</i>

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:49.800
<i>"Me too!"</i>

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.570
"Same here!"

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:51.940
<i>"Nakajima!"</i>

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.270
<i>"W... Wait a sec!"</i>

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.470
I won't let you get away
with this, Strike Man!

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.550
I'll catch you
myself!

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.090
Close enough!

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.130
Damn!

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:20.030
Natsumi, we're going
after him!

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:20.830
Okay!

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:26.370
Huh? Strike Man?

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.840
In like a flash! Out
like a flash!

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:31.910
The Superhero Strike
Man is here!

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:36.920
Strike Shots!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.520
Never jump the tracks if you
can't take some whacks!

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:58.070
Hey!

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:00.840
Are you okay?

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:01.940
Yeah. I think so...

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:03.770
Can you chase him on your Moto-Compo?

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.410
Okay!

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:18.720
There he is!

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.430
Hmm... It's a race.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.360
I can't keep up with
him on this thing.

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:31.440
And he's a pretty
good rider.

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:35.600
Nakajima?!

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.010
Hey, leave the
rest to me!

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:40.770
Go for it! This is your chance
for vindication!

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.610
That creep!

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:47.580
A cop, huh? In
that case...

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:53.090
In the name of justice!
Strike Sliding Turn!

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:02.790
He's got some nerve! Is
he a freak or what?!

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:03.600
Whoa!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:09.470
Hey, lady!

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:15.110
Hey, lady! Get out
of my way!

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.580
You little
wimp!

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.590
That damned Strike Man!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:28.260
It's too bad... we
almost got him.

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:31.330
Damn! How dare he
insult me like that?!

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:36.370
Well, at least we know that Nakajima
is definitely not the Strike Man.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.130
What did I
tell ya!

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:41.540
Come on, let's not go
on about that...

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:43.940
Huh?

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.740
I think I've got
an idea!

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:50.920
Where next?

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:53.090
Wha... m'drunk...

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.520
What're you sayin'?

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:56.180
Dunno... huh?

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:59.020
Oh, corrupted drunkards, your
presence offends the world!

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:01.790
Behold! The Superhero
Strike Man is here!

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:05.760
Hey, Miyuki, Nakajima's sure
getting into the act.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:09.230
Strike!

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:13.770
Press-on Punishment
Stickers!

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:19.070
Those who drink and cause
public disturbances...

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:22.150
The Strike Man shall
punish thee!

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:34.490
He's here.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.120
Where?!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:39.560
Too soft. You're too soft,
you Strike Man lmposter!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.660
There he is!

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:44.390
Evil must be dealt with
more severely.

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:53.100
Strike Ball of
Punishment!

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:59.310
I knew you'd show
up, Strike Man!

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:01.680
You... You caught my
Ball of Justice!

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:04.690
Give it up!

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.220
It's one thing to be a defender
of justice...

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.950
...but what you are
doing is criminal!

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:12.790
Thanks for your help
the other day.

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:15.700
I'll always keep your autographed
ball as a memento.

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:18.700
Prepare yourself...

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:22.170
Oh, the grief I've suffered,
because of you!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:35.680
I suppose the time has come for
me to remove my arm guards.

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:38.450
What?!

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:42.220
These Strike Arm Guards are designed
to regulate my power.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.920
Made of ultra-tempered steel, they
weigh a total of 80 kilograms!

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:56.300
He's just all bark
and no bite.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:59.780
Silence! Silence! There is
a method in my justice!

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:04.180
This is a challenge!
You and me...

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.780
Let's see who has the stronger
spirit of justice!

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:10.650
Sounds interesting!
I accept!

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:20.190
Come on,
let's go!

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.600
She's a tough
one!

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:24.430
Wha!?

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:31.480
She thinks she can
hit a home run?

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:37.480
lmpertinent woman!

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:39.550
One-ball duel!

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:44.860
Natsumi!

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:46.920
Natsumi!
Leave this to me.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:51.960
My Shining Strike
Ball!

00:19:52.270 --> 00:19:52.900
Aah!

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:54.420
Aah!
This is new!

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:57.930
See if you can
hit this one!

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:10.780
I'll show
you...

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:22.150
...the real power
of justice!

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:35.130
My only ball
of justice...

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:37.880
A perfect hit!

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.170
A perfect hit!
Natsumi!

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:45.370
My... My spirit of justice
wasn't strong enough?

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:51.650
That was a good pitch,
Strike Man.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:21:06.330
I...

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:10.900
I shall invigorate my spirit, and
challenge you once again!

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:13.410
We shall meet again,
Home Run Girl!

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.350
Who ya calling Home Run Girl?!

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:18.080
Come on, let's get him!

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:20.050
Gotcha!
Come on, let's get him!

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:24.060
He's done it to us again!

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:25.960
He's done it to us again!
He's a sneaky devil, isn't he?

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:34.530
How dare y'cut me
off... you idiot...

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:37.430
The gift from heaven
to earth...

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:39.830
The sworn enemy of
evil, Strike Man!

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:43.600
The one who answers the cries
of justice! I have returned!

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:45.610
Yeah!

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:49.670
Long live justice!

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:11.470
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:20.040
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me Ionely.</i>

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:31.090
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:39.130
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:47.970
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:56.880
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:57.180 --> 00:23:04.410
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:12.060
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:16.070 --> 00:23:17.230
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:25.310
"Lucky Woman"

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:27.080
Natsumi... Miyuki...

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:30.980
I heard about a former classmate, Sagami-
Ono, who has a grudge against you.

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:32.390
You're gossiping again.

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:32.780
Wait... Wait...

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:36.580
No! I don't think she can stand the
fact I graduated top of the class.

00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:37.690
Top of your class?

00:23:37.690 --> 00:23:39.210
Well, I just lucked out on everything!

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.950
Aha, I think I know
how she feels.

00:23:42.130 --> 00:23:44.760
Miss Sagami-Ono, Miyuki
and I are on your side!

00:23:44.930 --> 00:23:46.870
Next time on You're Under Arrest, File 8,
"Big Duel for Lucky Yoriko."

